  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Ruins of 18th-Century and Other Structures on Bunce Island Associated with the Transatlantic Slave Trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As a major slave fort, Bunce Island was part of an economic and demographic dynamic that transformed Africa, the United States, the Caribbean, and Europe between the late 17th and early 19th centuries. This project, which involves conservation of the fort ruins and measures to reduce the risk of coastal erosion, directly supports the U.S. embassys efforts to support economic development and recovery in the aftermath of the 2014 Ebola virus outbreak.</narrative>
  </description>
